{"toolCallId":"call_c0ee0a99ce564832abed62deb910aea1","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wfeb6409c4f/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.2 -->\n# Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path)`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the argument loop, `show_help()` option block, output dispatch, final `exit 0` and trailing exit-code comment block in the target script, and confirm each anchor this plan names still exists (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T002 [P] Capture baseline report output in text and JSON modes for one fixture folder, to diff against after the change (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T003 [P] Confirm the Bash 3.2 constraint and that the percentage is already an integer before any comparison, so the gate needs no `bc` call (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 Add a `MIN_PERCENT=\"\"` global to the globals block, beside `VERBOSE`, `JSON_OUTPUT`, `QUALITY_CHECK`, `SINGLE_FILE` and `SPEC_FOLDER` (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T005 Add the `--min-percent)` case to the argument loop, capturing the next argument and shifting by two (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T006 Validate the captured value as an integer in 0-100 and reject a missing value, a non-integer, a negative and a value above 100 with a stderr usage line and `exit 1` (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T007 Derive the gate percentage from the value the report prints: `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE` in folder mode, the sourced stats-file `percentage` with the output path's existing fallback in `--file` mode (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T008 Add the threshold comparison after the output dispatch and before the final exit, written as a full `if` block so `errexit` cannot turn the false branch into an early exit, and exit 3 only when the percentage is strictly below `MIN_PERCENT` (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T009 List `--min-percent <N>` in `show_help()` and on the header `# Options:` line, stating the exit-3 condition (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T010 Document exit code 3 in the trailing exit-code comment block, keeping the comment durable and free of packet or requirement identifiers (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T011 Add vitest cases for below-threshold, at-threshold, invalid value and unchanged report output (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts`)\n- [ ] T012 Add a vitest case for single-file mode, asserting the verdict follows that file's `completion_percentage` (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts`)\n- [ ] T013 Run the vitest file and confirm the two existing cases plus the new ones all pass (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts`)\n- [ ] T014 Diff text and JSON report output with and without `--min-percent` and confirm no difference, then confirm the unchanged exit codes 0 and 1 on the success and error paths (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T015 Confirm `--help` lists the option and still exits 0 (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.2 -->\n# Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path)`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the argument loop, `show_help()` option block, output dispatch, final `exit 0` and trailing exit-code comment block in the target script, and confirm each anchor this plan names still exists (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T002 [P] Capture baseline report output in text and JSON modes for one fixture folder, to diff against after the change (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T003 [P] Confirm the Bash 3.2 constraint and that the percentage is already an integer before any comparison, so the gate needs no `bc` call (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 Add a `MIN_PERCENT=\"\"` global to the globals block, beside `VERBOSE`, `JSON_OUTPUT`, `QUALITY_CHECK`, `SINGLE_FILE` and `SPEC_FOLDER` (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T005 Add the `--min-percent)` case to the argument loop, capturing the next argument and shifting by two (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T006 Validate the captured value as an integer in 0-100 and reject a missing value, a non-integer, a negative and a value above 100 with a stderr usage line and `exit 1` (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T007 Derive the gate percentage from the value the report prints: `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE` in folder mode, the sourced stats-file `percentage` with the output path's existing fallback in `--file` mode (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T008 Add the threshold comparison after the output dispatch and before the final exit, written as a full `if` block so `errexit` cannot turn the false branch into an early exit, and exit 3 only when the percentage is strictly below `MIN_PERCENT` (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T009 List `--min-percent <N>` in `show_help()` and on the header `# Options:` line, stating the exit-3 condition (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T010 Document exit code 3 in the trailing exit-code comment block, keeping the comment durable and free of packet or requirement identifiers (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T016 Emit a boolean `min_percent_met` in the JSON document when `--json` and `--min-percent` are combined, true when Overall Completion is at or above `N` and false otherwise, and omit it when `--min-percent` is absent (REQ-008) (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T011 Add vitest cases for below-threshold, at-threshold, invalid value and unchanged report output (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts`)\n- [ ] T012 Add a vitest case for single-file mode, asserting the verdict follows that file's `completion_percentage` (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts`)\n- [ ] T013 Run the vitest file and confirm the two existing cases plus the new ones all pass (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts`)\n- [ ] T014 Diff text and JSON report output with and without `--min-percent` and confirm no difference, then confirm the unchanged exit codes 0 and 1 on the success and error paths (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T015 Confirm `--help` lists the option and still exits 0 (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":1,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":0}}],"locations":[{"path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wfeb6409c4f/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wfeb6409c4f/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"edit"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_e786511dc97241ea8090e56966b8ee3c","title":"Ran bash","kind":"execute","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"resource","resource":{"mimeType":"text/x-shellscript","text":"bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent --strict","uri":"tool://preview"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/preview_is_shell_command":true}}}],"rawInput":{"command":"bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent --strict","workdir":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wfeb6409c4f/tree"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/commandNames":["bash"],"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_ecc15c24a47e4db194147e8a905c368f","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wfeb6409c4f/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/spec.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"calculate-completeness.sh computes a completion percentage but always exits 0, so a caller that needs a threshold has to parse its text or JSON output. A --min-percent <N> option lets the caller gate on that percentage with one flag and an exit-status check, while the report itself stays byte-identical.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent\"\n  - \"add a min percent option to calculate completeness\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core | v2.2 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 1 |\n| **Priority** | P1 |\n| **Status** | Planned |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-26 |\n| **Branch** | detached HEAD (packet created with `--skip-branch`) |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\n`calculate-completeness.sh` already knows the one number a caller wants: it prints `Overall Completion: <N>%` in text mode and `\"overall_completion\": <N>` in JSON mode, then ends with an unconditional `exit 0`. A caller that needs to know whether a packet clears a threshold therefore has to capture stdout and parse it, and that parsing differs per output mode (`--json`, `--verbose`, `--file`) and per locale-sensitive status word. Every such caller re-implements the same fragile extraction, and a text-format change breaks them silently.\n\n### Purpose\nA caller passes `--min-percent <N>` once and branches on the exit status, so \"is this packet at least N% complete?\" becomes a single command with no stdout parsing, and the report it already prints is unchanged.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n\n### In Scope\n- Parse `--min-percent <N>` (long form, space-separated value) in the existing argument loop, alongside `--verbose`, `--json`, `--quality` and `--file`.\n- Reject an invalid `N` — non-integer, negative, greater than 100, or a missing value — with a usage error on stderr and exit 1.\n- Apply the threshold after the report is written: exit 3 when the reported completion percentage is below `N`, exit 0 otherwise. A percentage exactly equal to `N` passes.\n- Apply the same gate in text mode, JSON mode, and `--file` single-file mode.\n- List the option in the `show_help()` output and the header `# Options:` line, and document exit code 3 in the trailing exit-code comment block.\n\n\"Output is unchanged\" here means the completeness report — the text block and the JSON document. The `--help` listing and the header comment gain the new option, which is the only user-visible text difference.\n\n### Out of Scope\n- The `--min-percent=<N>` equals form and a short alias such as `-m` — not requested; the space-separated long form is enough for a first version.\n- Any change to the percentages, status words, JSON keys, or per-file breakdown the report already prints.\n- Gating on individual per-file percentages in `--verbose` mode — only the percentage the report presents as the overall result is compared.\n- Changing the existing exit codes 0 (success) and 1 (error), or the error paths that produce them.\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh` | Modify | Option parsing, `N` validation, threshold gate, help and exit-code documentation |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts` | Modify | Cases for pass, below-threshold, invalid value, and unchanged report output |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-001 | `--min-percent <N>` is accepted without changing the report | stdout and stderr for `--json <folder>` are byte-identical to `--json <folder> --min-percent 0`; same comparison in text mode with `diff` reporting no difference |\n| REQ-002 | Exit 3 when the reported completion is below `N` | On a fixture whose report says `Overall Completion: 80%`, `--min-percent 81` exits 3 |\n| REQ-003 | Exit 0 when the reported completion is at or above `N` | On the same 80% fixture, `--min-percent 80` and `--min-percent 0` both exit 0 |\n| REQ-004 | Behavior without the option is untouched | The two existing cases in `calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts` pass without edits; a missing folder still exits 1 and a valid folder still exits 0 |\n| REQ-005 | Invalid `N` is a usage error, never a threshold verdict | `--min-percent abc`, `--min-percent -1`, `--min-percent 101` and a trailing `--min-percent` with no value each exit 1 with a message on stderr |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-006 | The gate covers `--file` and `--json` modes using the percentage the report presents | A single file reporting `Completion: 80%` exits 3 with `--min-percent 81` and 0 with `--min-percent 80`; the JSON mode verdict matches the text mode verdict for the same fixture |\n| REQ-007 | The option is discoverable | `--help` output contains `--min-percent` and states the exit-3 condition |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: A caller gates on completion with one flag and one exit-status comparison, with no stdout parsing.\n- **SC-002**: For a given folder state, the report bytes are identical with and without the option, in both text and JSON modes.\n- **SC-003**: The script's exit-status vocabulary stays unambiguous: 0 means success and at-or-above threshold, 1 means it could not run, 3 means it ran and the result is below the threshold.\n- **SC-004**: `npx vitest run .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts --config .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/vitest.config.ts --project cli` passes with the new cases included.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | `bc`, already required by the script | None new — the script aborts with a clear error if `bc` is absent | The comparison itself is integer-only, so the gate adds no `bc` call |\n| Risk | `set -euo pipefail` at the top of the script | A bare `[[ ... ]]` test as the last command of a branch can exit early before the report is written; the file already documents this at the percentage clamp | Write the gate as a full `if` block and keep an explicit `exit` as the script's last statement |\n| Risk | Comparing the wrong percentage in `--file` mode | The verdict disagrees with the number the report printed | Derive the gate value from the same source the output path uses, rather than recomputing it |\n| Risk | An invalid `N` surfacing as 3 | \"Below threshold\" and \"bad input\" become indistinguishable to a caller | Validate `N` during argument parsing, before any calculation, and exit 1 there |\n| Risk | Bash 3.2 compatibility | A construct such as `${var,,}` or an associative array fails on the macOS system bash | Keep to `[[ =~ ]]`, integer comparison, and the globals the script already declares |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 7. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\nNone blocking. One interpretive decision was made during authoring and is worth confirming before implementation:\n\n- The request says the script exits 3 when \"its Overall Completion\" is below `N`. In `--file` mode the report has no `Overall Completion` line — it prints `Completion: <N>%` for that one file. REQ-006 reads the rule as \"the percentage the report presents as the result\", so `--file` plus `--min-percent` gates on the single file. If the intent was folder-only gating, the alternative is to reject the combination as a usage error (exit 1) instead.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"calculate-completeness.sh computes a completion percentage but always exits 0, so a caller that needs a threshold has to parse its text or JSON output. A --min-percent <N> option lets the caller gate on that percentage with one flag and an exit-status check, while the report itself stays byte-identical.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent\"\n  - \"add a min percent option to calculate completeness\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core | v2.2 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 1 |\n| **Priority** | P1 |\n| **Status** | Planned |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-26 |\n| **Branch** | detached HEAD (packet created with `--skip-branch`) |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\n`calculate-completeness.sh` already knows the one number a caller wants: it prints `Overall Completion: <N>%` in text mode and `\"overall_completion\": <N>` in JSON mode, then ends with an unconditional `exit 0`. A caller that needs to know whether a packet clears a threshold therefore has to capture stdout and parse it, and that parsing differs per output mode (`--json`, `--verbose`, `--file`) and per locale-sensitive status word. Every such caller re-implements the same fragile extraction, and a text-format change breaks them silently.\n\n### Purpose\nA caller passes `--min-percent <N>` once and branches on the exit status, so \"is this packet at least N% complete?\" becomes a single command with no stdout parsing, and the report it already prints is unchanged.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n\n### In Scope\n- Parse `--min-percent <N>` (long form, space-separated value) in the existing argument loop, alongside `--verbose`, `--json`, `--quality` and `--file`.\n- Reject an invalid `N` — non-integer, negative, greater than 100, or a missing value — with a usage error on stderr and exit 1.\n- Apply the threshold after the report is written: exit 3 when the reported completion percentage is below `N`, exit 0 otherwise. A percentage exactly equal to `N` passes.\n- Apply the same gate in text mode, JSON mode, and `--file` single-file mode.\n- List the option in the `show_help()` output and the header `# Options:` line, and document exit code 3 in the trailing exit-code comment block.\n\n\"Output is unchanged\" here means the completeness report — the text block and the JSON document. The `--help` listing and the header comment gain the new option, which is the only user-visible text difference.\n\n### Out of Scope\n- The `--min-percent=<N>` equals form and a short alias such as `-m` — not requested; the space-separated long form is enough for a first version.\n- Any change to the percentages, status words, JSON keys, or per-file breakdown the report already prints.\n- Gating on individual per-file percentages in `--verbose` mode — only the percentage the report presents as the overall result is compared.\n- Changing the existing exit codes 0 (success) and 1 (error), or the error paths that produce them.\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh` | Modify | Option parsing, `N` validation, threshold gate, help and exit-code documentation |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts` | Modify | Cases for pass, below-threshold, invalid value, and unchanged report output |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-001 | `--min-percent <N>` is accepted without changing the report | stdout and stderr for `--json <folder>` are byte-identical to `--json <folder> --min-percent 0`; same comparison in text mode with `diff` reporting no difference |\n| REQ-002 | Exit 3 when the reported completion is below `N` | On a fixture whose report says `Overall Completion: 80%`, `--min-percent 81` exits 3 |\n| REQ-003 | Exit 0 when the reported completion is at or above `N` | On the same 80% fixture, `--min-percent 80` and `--min-percent 0` both exit 0 |\n| REQ-004 | Behavior without the option is untouched | The two existing cases in `calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts` pass without edits; a missing folder still exits 1 and a valid folder still exits 0 |\n| REQ-005 | Invalid `N` is a usage error, never a threshold verdict | `--min-percent abc`, `--min-percent -1`, `--min-percent 101` and a trailing `--min-percent` with no value each exit 1 with a message on stderr |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-006 | The gate covers `--file` and `--json` modes using the percentage the report presents | A single file reporting `Completion: 80%` exits 3 with `--min-percent 81` and 0 with `--min-percent 80`; the JSON mode verdict matches the text mode verdict for the same fixture |\n| REQ-007 | The option is discoverable | `--help` output contains `--min-percent` and states the exit-3 condition |\n| REQ-008 | `--json` with `--min-percent` carries the verdict in the JSON document | With `--json --min-percent <N>`, the JSON output gains a boolean `min_percent_met` that is `true` when Overall Completion is at or above `N` and `false` when it is below; the field is absent when `--min-percent` is not passed |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: A caller gates on completion with one flag and one exit-status comparison, with no stdout parsing.\n- **SC-002**: For a given folder state, the report bytes are identical with and without the option, in both text and JSON modes.\n- **SC-003**: The script's exit-status vocabulary stays unambiguous: 0 means success and at-or-above threshold, 1 means it could not run, 3 means it ran and the result is below the threshold.\n- **SC-004**: `npx vitest run .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/calculate-completeness-script.vitest.ts --config .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/vitest.config.ts --project cli` passes with the new cases included.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | `bc`, already required by the script | None new — the script aborts with a clear error if `bc` is absent | The comparison itself is integer-only, so the gate adds no `bc` call |\n| Risk | `set -euo pipefail` at the top of the script | A bare `[[ ... ]]` test as the last command of a branch can exit early before the report is written; the file already documents this at the percentage clamp | Write the gate as a full `if` block and keep an explicit `exit` as the script's last statement |\n| Risk | Comparing the wrong percentage in `--file` mode | The verdict disagrees with the number the report printed | Derive the gate value from the same source the output path uses, rather than recomputing it |\n| Risk | An invalid `N` surfacing as 3 | \"Below threshold\" and \"bad input\" become indistinguishable to a caller | Validate `N` during argument parsing, before any calculation, and exit 1 there |\n| Risk | Bash 3.2 compatibility | A construct such as `${var,,}` or an associative array fails on the macOS system bash | Keep to `[[ =~ ]]`, integer comparison, and the globals the script already declares |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 7. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\nNone blocking. One interpretive decision was made during authoring and is worth confirming before implementation:\n\n- The request says the script exits 3 when \"its Overall Completion\" is below `N`. In `--file` mode the report has no `Overall Completion` line — it prints `Completion: <N>%` for that one file. REQ-006 reads the rule as \"the percentage the report presents as the result\", so `--file` plus `--min-percent` gates on the single file. If the intent was folder-only gating, the alternative is to reject the combination as a usage error (exit 1) instead.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":1,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":0}}],"locations":[{"path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wfeb6409c4f/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/spec.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wfeb6409c4f/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/spec.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"edit"}}
